    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bq4",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "lq1",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://colorado.public.law/statutes/crs_13-21-201"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sq0",
          "text": "Colorado law limits who may bring a wrongful death claim, and the applicable rules shift depending on how much time has passed since the death. Under",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sq2",
          "text": " Colorado Revised Statutes Section 13-21-201",
          "marks": [
            "lq1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sq3",
          "text": ", eligibility to file breaks down as follows:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bq6",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sq5",
          "text": "During the first year after the death, only the surviving spouse holds the right to file, though the spouse may choose in writing to include the deceased’s children or other heirs in the action.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bq8",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sq7",
          "text": "During the second year, if the spouse does not file, or if no spouse survives, the deceased’s heirs may bring the claim.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bqa",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sq9",
          "text": "If the deceased leaves no spouse, children, or designated beneficiary, the deceased’s parents may step forward to pursue the claim on the family’s behalf.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bqe",
      "style": "normal",
