  "faqs": [
    {
      "_key": "q1",
      "question": "Does it matter if my loved one was partly at fault for the accident?",
      "answer": [
        {
          "_type": "block",
          "_key": "bsj",
          "style": "normal",
          "markDefs": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "ssi",
              "text": "Colorado follows a modified comparative negligence rule, meaning a family may still recover compensation even if the deceased shared some fault, as long as that share stays below 50 percent. Any recovery is reduced in proportion to the assigned percentage of fault.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "q2",
      "question": "How much does it cost to hire a wrongful death lawyer in Greeley?",
      "answer": [
        {
          "_type": "block",
          "_key": "bsn",
          "style": "normal",
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "lsk",
              "_type": "link",
              "href": "/"
            }
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "ssl",
              "text": "Dormer Harpring ",
              "marks": [
                "lsk",
                "strong"
              ]
            },
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "ssm",
              "text": "works on a contingency fee basis, meaning families pay no upfront cost and no legal fee unless we recover compensation. We also advance the cost of expert witnesses without charging interest.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "q3",
      "question": "Can a wrongful death claim move forward if criminal charges are also pending?",
      "answer": [
        {
          "_type": "block",
          "_key": "bsp",
          "style": "normal",
          "markDefs": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "sso",
              "text": "Yes, a wrongful death claim is a separate civil action from any criminal case tied to the same death. The two proceed independently, and the outcome of one does not determine the outcome of the other.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "q4",
      "question": "How is compensation divided among multiple surviving family members?",
      "answer": [
        {
          "_type": "block",
          "_key": "bsr",
          "style": "normal",
          "markDefs": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "ssq",
              "text": "When several family members share the right to file, such as a spouse and children, compensation is typically divided by agreement or, if the case goes to trial, by the jury. An attorney can help ensure the division reflects each person’s actual loss.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "q5",
      "question": "How long does a wrongful death case in Greeley typically take to resolve?",
      "answer": [
        {
          "_type": "block",
          "_key": "bst",
          "style": "normal",
          "markDefs": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "sss",
              "text": "Timelines vary based on how quickly liability is established and whether the insurer disputes fault. Straightforward cases may resolve in several months, while contested or complex cases can take a year or longer, particularly if the case goes to trial.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "q6",
      "question": "What should I do immediately after a fatal accident in Greeley?",
      "answer": [
        {
          "_type": "block",
          "_key": "bsx",
          "style": "normal",
          "markDefs": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "ssu",
              "text": "Contact law enforcement to ensure an official report is filed, and reach out for support with any immediate needs the family may have, as such action also helps avoid giving a recorded statement to an insurance company before speaking with a lawyer. A ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "ssv",
              "text": "Greeley wrongful death lawyer",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ]
            },
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "ssw",
              "text": " can help protect the family’s interests and preserve evidence that a future claim may depend on.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "q7",
      "question": "What evidence is most important in a Greeley wrongful death case?",
      "answer": [
        {
          "_type": "block",
          "_key": "bsz",
          "style": "normal",
          "markDefs": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "_type": "span",
              "_key": "ssy",
              "text": "Police reports, medical and autopsy records, witness statements, and any available photographs or surveillance footage all play a central role. Evidence like this can disappear quickly, which is why gathering it soon after the accident matters.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
